    "result_text": "All tests pass. Let me confirm the full change set is complete and coherent.\n\nThe implementation is done and the build is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes, kept as small cohesive edits:\n\n**Behaviour**\n- `DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `owner.setDeleted(true)` and `save`s, so `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` retains the row (still returns 204/2xx) and `GET` still finds it.\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` / `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 the create pipeline's two duplicate checks each gained a leading `!existing.isDeleted()` guard, so a soft-deleted owner no longer blocks a matching new create.\n\n**Model & persistence**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `boolean deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, defaults `false` for new owners) with one-line `isDeleted`/`setDeleted` accessors, avoiding growth of the existing large getter/setter block.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended `FALSE` to the 10 positional seed inserts to match the new column.\n\n**API surface**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so `GET` now reports `deleted` (`false` on create, `true` after delete). No mapper edit needed.\n\nNotes: only `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` and `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity` run in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline (the telephone/email checks aren't wired there), so those two fully cover the spec's \"duplicate and identity checks.\" The two acceptance tests \u2014 soft-delete flags-and-retains, and deleted-owner-ignored-by-duplicate-check \u2014 both pass.",
